{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123732","id":4606745370,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABEpVbGg","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123732","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123732.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123732.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123732","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123732/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123732/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123732/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e90b68ddab36bb1ece8a964b0ea79340d72a5a40","number":123732,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add support for Spatial pinch input on visionOS","user":{"login":"oPinon","id":5775700,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzU3MDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5775700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oPinon","html_url":"https://github.com/oPinon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oPinon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oPinon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oPinon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oPinon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oPinon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oPinon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oPinon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oPinon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oPinon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Feature\r\n\r\nThis pull request adds support for [Spatial Events](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/compositorservices/layerrenderer/onspatialevent-2jg60) from visionOS (when you look at your game and pinch and/or drag).\r\n\r\nHere is a demo project using the feature in Godot:\r\n[spatial-events.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32781027/spatial-events.zip)\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c1fb186b-537b-4eaf-80c9-6345498428cb\r\n\r\nThe events map to [XRController3D](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_xrcontroller3d.html) nodes:\r\n\r\n| XRController3D tracker name | Data | Actions |\r\n| - | - | - |\r\n| \"left_hand\" | Transform of the left hand while pinching; or left PSVR2 controller if held | \"trigger_click\" |\r\n| \"right_hand\" | Transform of the right hand while pinching; or right PSVR2 controller if held | \"trigger_click\" |\r\n| \"/user/eyes_ext\" | Eye ray from the last pinch (either from left or right hand, depending on which was the latest) | none |\r\n\r\nPinch events are sent as \"trigger_click\" actions on \"left_hand\" and \"right_hand\".\r\n\r\n<img width=\"952\" height=\"536\" alt=\"XRController3D mapping\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/246e284f-b720-4b1f-bdef-285850a5e270\" />\r\n\r\n### Ray\r\n\r\nThe \"/user/eyes_ext\" starts from your head and goes towards the direction that you are looking at. It only moves during the initial pinch and does not move while you drag. The ray goes towards -Z, relative to the controller.\r\n\r\n### Pinch\r\n\r\nThe \"left_hand\" and \"right_hand\" follow your hand. You can combine them with the ray above to implement drag gestures.\r\n\r\n## Compatibility with hand tracking and controller tracking\r\n\r\nNote that this is compatible with hand tracking and controller tracking, but does not require them.\r\n\r\nThis PR shares the same trackers used for [PSVR2 controller tracking](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122567) (\"left_hand\" and \"right_hand\"), but dynamically switches between the two during a pinch.\r\n\r\nHere is a video showing that controller tracking still works:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/226320b3-b5bd-4540-aea6-ac6d0ffa4b3b\r\n\r\n## Differences with other platforms\r\n\r\nThis PR tries to map the [visionOS API](https://developer.apple.com/documentation/compositorservices/layerrenderer/onspatialevent-2jg60) to existing Godot concepts, but it is not a 1-1 match. While visionOS also supports hand tracking and controller tracking, the \"spatial events\" are the default interaction model, and work a bit differently: the main difference is using eye tracking to target objects in the scene or target the UI, combined with hand tracking to do various gestures.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":865585000,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4NjU1ODUwMDA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:xr","name":"topic:xr","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9548448620,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAACOSHDbA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:visionos","name":"platform:visionos","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","number":25,"state":"open","title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"l